WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.773
DTG white-ink control supports
multiple fabric colors.

2
00:00:03.773 --> 00:00:09.998
Here we use the same color artwork to demonstrate
white-ink settings for different garments.

3
00:00:10.753 --> 00:00:18.219
The panel provides ten preset colors, plus a custom color
option and color picking from the artwork.

4
00:00:18.219 --> 00:00:20.011
First choose red fabric.

5
00:00:20.011 --> 00:00:22.251
The color artwork is retained.

6
00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:29.075
White-ink amounts are controlled separately for areas close to
the fabric color and for the rest of the

7
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:29.563
artwork.

8
00:00:29.563 --> 00:00:32.249
Here they are set to five and fifty percent.

9
00:00:34.387 --> 00:00:36.365
Click Generate DTG Artwork.

10
00:00:36.365 --> 00:00:43.619
The software performs the actual processing through
Photoshop and saves a TIFF with the W1 channel.

11
00:00:43.987 --> 00:00:50.044
Use the actual color output to inspect the print, and the
white-ink preview to inspect coverage.

12
00:00:50.044 --> 00:00:54.524
The red matching areas and the other colors
can be compared separately.

13
00:00:57.187 --> 00:01:00.399
Change the fabric to green and generate again.

14
00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:06.264
The artwork colors remain, while white ink is
recalculated for the new fabric color.

15
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:14.086
Review the output for the selected fabric and production
needs, then send the finished artwork directly

16
00:01:14.086 --> 00:01:15.203
to DTG placement.
